 description: "Ubuntu Server 24.04 (SSH): blind-keystroke-dismiss GRUB (OCR-free), then drive everything else over SSH once cloud-init has finished bringing up sshd."
 keystrokeMechanism: ssh
@@ -34,6 +34,22 @@ component:
     name: Enter
     description: "Blind-dismiss the GRUB boot menu (retry)"
 
+  # Subiquity DOES stop for confirmation on this guest: New-VM.ps1 boots the
+  # live-server ISO with a CIDATA seed CD and deliberately does NOT put
+  # 'autoinstall' on the kernel command line (see its .DESCRIPTION -- the
+  # pre-baked cloud image is rejected precisely BECAUSE it skips this prompt).
+  # So the installer parks on "Continue with autoinstall? (yes|no)" and nothing
+  # in this sequence answers it -- sshd never starts and step sshWaitReady burns
+  # its full 2400 s. The gui sibling (start.guest.ubuntu.server.24.yml) has
+  # always carried this step; the ssh variant was missing it.
+  # OCR is already a dependency of this sequence (sshWaitReady's
+  # installerFailurePatterns scan frames the same way), so this costs no new one.
+  - action: waitForAndEnter
+    pattern: "Continue with autoinstall?"
+    timeoutSeconds: 900
+    text: "yes"
+    description: "OCR: Continue with autoinstall?"
+
   - action: sshWaitReady
     timeoutSeconds: 2400
